{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos","id":1387060,"title":"Mythos","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-09T13:23:20-07:00","id":1387060,"title":"Mythos","content":"Hello all.<br /> <br /> I was reading some tales from Lovecraft, and suddenly I noticed a little issue on the kind of story I was thinking about when thinking about Masks of Mythos.<br /> <br /> When I think about Mythos, I usually think from a very human perspective, the view from characters that are investigating or facing somehow the truth that they are no more than dust in front of the old ones (or even some of the &quot;not so powerful&quot; other terrors).<br /> <br /> But if we are supposed to be Heros (or even more) against the old ones, we are probably going to have a much stronger position, maybe cutting Deep Ones as butter before reaching Dagon and Hydra, maybe even capable of facing somehow Hastur in the end of the story.<br /> <br /> I see no problem on that, but it's not how I (personally) would handle my Cosmic Horror story. I would probably work on a more horizontal development version of Storypath (TC in the case), and keep my characters pretty mortal.<br /> <br /> What are your plans on that? Do you think you would go on a Hero/Demigod grow or keep mortal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T19:51:28-07:00","id":1387160,"title":"","content":"If you read the Randolph Carter stories I think you could see him as becoming a Scion of Yog-Sothoth. The danger to those self-chosen to become Mythos Scions is insanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T16:05:21-07:00","id":1388175,"title":"","content":"One thing I am doing is the old ones, are what theAztec gods are fighting against. They are ancient foes of the gods, and there are sorcerers who call on them, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T16:50:57-07:00","id":1388185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1387160#post1387160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you read the Randolph Carter stories I think you could see him as becoming a Scion of Yog-Sothoth. The danger to those self-chosen to become Mythos Scions is insanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one kind of story to tell, for sure, and one that may be very interesting to deal with. Dealing with a Hero while becoming less human in both appearance and mentality must be a very interesting way to deal with it. The most interesting part is, some of the characters would not care about this taint, and will see it as good as becoming a Hero of other pantheons.<br /> <br /> Also, if you keep the game on Hero, and treat them as prophets or powerful cultists of the old ones (what is pretty evil by the way... but ok) you have the same feeling of loosing humanity.<br /> <br /> But, as I said, it would lose a bit of the Cosmic Horror feeling, as you are the horror or at least see it as positive...<br /> <br /> Well that's the game I was planning for Mythos, one with investigation or at least diving into cosmic horror from the human perspective, not the only one that can be played on Lovecraft Country.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there is this new series Lovecraft Country that is coming on HBO or Amazon, can't remember, and I am a bit anxious for some horror in my soul lasting for more than a few hour since the 6th season of American Horror Story (the last one that brought this feeling).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T00:14:33-07:00","id":1388255,"title":"","content":"Masks of the Mythos is meant to be a Shard... it is set in a version of the World where the other Pantheons do not exist, so it would not be surprising if the basic assumptions of Heroes (if they're even called that) and what they can do are significantly different as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T12:55:11-07:00","id":1388399,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t wait for Masks of the Mythos, but why can\u2019t I use the Mythos in conjunction with the other pantheons? They don\u2019t really contradict each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T13:04:00-07:00","id":1388403,"title":"","content":"They kind of do, in much the same way that true monotheism contradicts Scion. Specifically, the Mythos makes assumptions about the nature of the universe that conflict with the assumptions that the rest of the Pantheons are based on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T13:25:10-07:00","id":1388409,"title":"","content":"As I see, rulewise they must work together with no issue, or at least be coherent.<br /> <br /> Settingwise, they are almost completely contradictory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T13:57:56-07:00","id":1388421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388399#post1388399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can\u2019t wait for Masks of the Mythos, but why can\u2019t I use the Mythos in conjunction with the other pantheons? They don\u2019t really contradict each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure with enough tweaking (which could be no tweaking at all, I don't know how the mechanics work) you could use them together in your games... but setting wise the Mythos 'deities' don't really fit... they're utterly unconcerned with Humanity, which is one of the prime hallmarks of Godhood in base Scion, and are harmful enough to Humanity (deliberately or not) that any Pantheon that even vaguely cares about people (which is pretty much all of them, but especially ones like the Teotl Deva or Orisha) would have wiped them out ages ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T15:43:35-07:00","id":1388466,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a> maybe they\u2019re too powerful to wipe out. The Old Ones have been imprisoned for thousands of years. Maybe the human pantheons were the ones who imprisoned them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T19:32:35-07:00","id":1388534,"title":"","content":"I am interested in seeing if I can use Mythos to show me how I could create Titan based Scions and not just Titanspawn. This would make the war even worse or better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T21:56:41-07:00","id":1388564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388466#post1388466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a> The Old Ones have been imprisoned for thousands of years</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you listen to the Deva that wasn't even a previous age of humanity. According to the Deva, they've been around since the dawn of the universe, if not longer. And they're not the only ones who say &quot;We were around in an age before this lost echo of times past&quot;.<br /> <br /> I personally will be keeping the Mythos very separate from the mainline games because truth be told? Compared to the Gods of humanity, the Elder Gods of the Mythos are kinda chumps. Yeah, Azathoth can potentially unmake all of everything. Shiva sometimes tries that when he wakes up from a bender until his sister slaps him upside the head and tells him &quot;Not TODAY, you idiot&quot;<br /> <br /> Ancient malevolent demons from the stars above? The Teotl fight those every night, and they've been holding them at bay THIS long.<br /> <br /> Now granted I'm one of those killjoys who finds the Elder Gods to be really boring, so I admit I may not be giving them enough credit, but from what I know of their source material and the build-up since then... Yeah, they're powerful. To a human. But are they really that impressive when they're not bullies picking on small humans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T23:09:26-07:00","id":1388580,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know The Bifrost Incident by The Mechanisms? I think they did the mix of mythology and Lovecraft rather well. Even though I'm not really that fond of doing it in Scion to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","name":"BlackLotos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar50_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T00:38:11-07:00","id":1388592,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what the point is with Masks of the Mythos they are NOT crossing over with human mythology. That's like losing the entire unique selling point, might as well just play Call of Cthulhu in that case.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure why the Mythos would be contradictory in any way to mythology. To me the big horrible monsters of the mythos are basically a modern version of the Titans of ancient mythologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 05-15-2020, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T02:00:30-07:00","id":1388608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388564#post1388564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if you listen to the Deva that wasn't even a previous age of humanity. According to the Deva, they've been around since the dawn of the universe, if not longer. And they're not the only ones who say &amp;quot;We were around in an age before this lost echo of times past&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> I personally will be keeping the Mythos very separate from the mainline games because truth be told? Compared to the Gods of humanity, the Elder Gods of the Mythos are kinda chumps. Yeah, Azathoth can potentially unmake all of everything. Shiva sometimes tries that when he wakes up from a bender until his sister slaps him upside the head and tells him &amp;quot;Not TODAY, you idiot&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Ancient malevolent demons from the stars above? The Teotl fight those every night, and they've been holding them at bay THIS long.<br /> <br /> Now granted I'm one of those killjoys who finds the Elder Gods to be really boring, so I admit I may not be giving them enough credit, but from what I know of their source material and the build-up since then... Yeah, they're powerful. To a human. But are they really that impressive when they're not bullies picking on small humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the Deva could be wrong. Just cause a god says it doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s true.<br /> <br /> The part about Shiva is kind of funny, but I still disagree with you. The Old Ones of the Mythos are more like Titans or even Primordials than gods.<br /> <br /> Exactly! That totally fits. Why couldn\u2019t the Old Ones be the \u201cancient malevolent demons from the stars\u201d that the Teotl banished thousands of years ago?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I basically agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9849_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9849\" data-vbnamecard=\"9849\">Aristarkos</a>. I mean, in the end I\u2019m gonna do what I want (or at least I\u2019ll get whoever runs the game to do it if it\u2019s that important to me) and you\u2019re gonna do what you want, but I still think combining the Mythos with the pantheons is a valid idea.<br /> <br /> Sorry. I\u2019m half asleep, so this might seem a little disjointed lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T02:43:39-07:00","id":1388617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388534#post1388534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am interested in seeing if I can use Mythos to show me how I could create Titan based Scions and not just Titanspawn. This would make the war even worse or better.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Titanomachy book is already poised to give us rules for Titan Scions, as well as new Callings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T02:59:33-07:00","id":1388621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388608#post1388608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but the Deva could be wrong. Just cause a god says it doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s true.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deva are correct, just as the Theoi are correct and the Orisha are correct... All Myths Are True in Scion, it's a central conceit of the game... so yes, a day for Brahma Vishnu and Shiva is 4.32 Billion years, meaning a few thousand years is less time than it takes one of them to piss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388608#post1388608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The part about Shiva is kind of funny, but I still disagree with you. The Old Ones of the Mythos are more like Titans or even Primordials than gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are fairly chumps compared to the Gods... the Spear of Lugh guarantees Victory against any foe, a single stray Deva Astra can destroy the Universe, God creates eldritch abomination angels on a lark, he can get rid of them just as easily, Huitzilopochtli eats malevolent things from outer space for breakfast, Oludomare the all powerful and Nyame the all loving do not take kindly to beings that threaten humanity on this scale, and that's just them individually... Gods care about their people, even if only as foils and sources of service... a Pantheon of uninterested (and frankly uninteresting) beings that harm humanity by merely existing would be anathema to pretty much all of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388608#post1388608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly! That totally fits. Why couldn\u2019t the Old Ones be the \u201cancient malevolent demons from the stars\u201d that the Teotl banished thousands of years ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because we know who those are... they are the Tzitzimime, not the Mediocre Old Ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388608#post1388608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyway, I basically agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9849_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9849\" data-vbnamecard=\"9849\">Aristarkos</a>. I mean, in the end I\u2019m gonna do what I want (or at least I\u2019ll get whoever runs the game to do it if it\u2019s that important to me) and you\u2019re gonna do what you want, but I still think combining the Mythos with the pantheons is a valid idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with them as well, though mostly in the sense that I have never gotten why Masks of the Mythos is a thing... it makes zero sense as a part of the World, and is also fairly old hat as a concept by itself. I wish you luck in your games though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:18:25-07:00","id":1388627,"title":"","content":"I am interested in this book but for all the parts that wont have anything to do with the Old Ones XD<br /> <br /> I've heard that there would be some parts about investigations in Scion as well as advice on using a horror tone.<br /> <br /> As for mixing Mythos Old One and the Pantheons.<br /> The problem isnt in who could beat who really.<br /> We could be talking about X beating Y and Y beating X till the universe end and still not be close to really saying anything.<br /> The problem is that the Old Ones are written as they dont care about humanity.<br /> If you compare the threat of Apep who wants to eat the Sun and Chtuhullu who doesnt want anything and isnt interested in interacting with mortals in any way.<br /> Then the Cosmic Horror who is important in a story isnt gonna be the Old One here.<br /> <br /> But and heres the important thing for me. Its being made because the mythos is popular. So if its popular then its gonna make alot of people happy and im happy with that.<br /> <br /> And who knows maybe people will talk about their games using the Mythos and its gonna spark something useful i hadnt considered before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T07:57:12-07:00","id":1388679,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a> I hate that conceit!!! Literally gives me a headache trying to figure it out. If I ever ran Scion, my version would be \u201cThe World exists independently of the pantheons. They may SAY they created the world, but they didn\u2019t. Everything else is (mostly) true, but only in that pantheon\u2019s geographic area of influence.\u201d<br /> <br /> Again, I don\u2019t take those claims literally. \u201cGuarantees victory against any foe\u201d is just Tuatha puffing (means exaggerated claims in advertising).<br /> <br /> Maybe Tzitzimime is just the name for the Old Ones in Nahuatl...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11312_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11312\" data-vbnamecard=\"11312\">Maitrecorbo</a> really? I thought the Old Ones hated humans and were trying to spread misery, horror and destruction by their very presence in the World.<br /> <br /> In the books the Old Ones were banished or imprisoned by beings called the elder gods. Those could be the pantheons, or at least their predecessors.<br /> <br /> Just saying...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T08:05:55-07:00","id":1388682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388679#post1388679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, I don\u2019t take those claims literally. \u201cGuarantees victory against any foe\u201d is just Tuatha puffing (means exaggerated claims in advertising).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And here is my problem.<br /> Why is the Tuatha claim of &quot;Guarantees victory against any foe&quot; just an exaggeration and the claim &quot;If Azathoth wakes up it unmakes the universe&quot; decided to be true?<br /> <br /> Either it all is, or you have made specific choices on what is true and what isnt.<br /> \u200b( I hope i'm not sounding too antagonistic here <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> . If so then i apologise)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T08:48:16-07:00","id":1388694,"title":"","content":"The idea of \u201cgranting victory against any foe\u201d or \u201chitting any target no matter the distance\u201d or \u201cdestroying anyone with a single hit\u201d or anything like this is an exaggeration from the point of view of a mortal (or at least silly from the point of view of a RPG).<br /> <br /> When competing with other gods, those effects are no more than scale.<br /> <br /> Azathoth is the \u201cleader\u201c of the Mythos Pantheon, and so has Legend 12, probably capable of beating almost any god when dealig on its purview, the same for Zeus, Odin, etc. According to its purview, it can mean almost anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T09:36:38-07:00","id":1388704,"title":"","content":"I admit my indifference towards the figures of the Mythos is like... What have they DONE other than give vague nightmares to people who ate too much shellfish before bed? If their major Thing is &quot;These things are big and unknowable and we're beneath them&quot;... So? That's really boring. What do they DO?<br /> <br /> Like, Shiva is set to unmake the universe so that Brahma can make it anew when the time is right. The Netjer maintain order and protect the sun every night. The Theoi are universal concepts that sometimes wear human suits.<br /> <br /> The Gods of humanity are SO MUCH more interesting, varied, menacing, frightening, enlightening, active, and loving than anything in the Cthulhu Mythos. Because they do things other than Vaguely Exist, Menacingly. Like, what do the Mythos bring that can't be done better with other Pantheons?<br /> <br /> Aside from maybe bring in some tentacles, but I think there'll be Gods in the Atua who'll have you covered if you like tentacles.<br /> <br /> Now I'll probably use the rules in the Mythos book. Not for the Mythos, but because I'm working on a writeup for the Powers from The Magnus Archive which I find actually interesting, and take a more active (if antagonistic) role in the overall plot. Yeah, they still don't work if you bring them into a setting with other Gods because that completely defangs the Cosmic Horror aspect of the setting, but at least they have themes, tendencies, and motifs.<br /> <br /> Edit: And to be clear I'm not saying &quot;Don't do this&quot;, I'm just saying &quot;I personally won't do this for these reasons&quot;. I can't stop you from doing a darn thing. Even if I think going &quot;Yeah well most of the Pantheons are liars and talk a big game&quot; is kind of a boring way out.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Actually I just noticed this-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything else is (mostly) true, but only in that pantheon\u2019s geographic area of influence</div> </div> </div> </div>... WHAT Geographic areas of influence? Do you region-lock your Pantheons in play? I don't. The Gods have worshippers everywhere. Sure, they may have more worshippers in certain places, but Thor doesn't get any less Thor when he's in Canada. And what about the worshippers of the Kami in Brazil? Do their prayers go unanswered just because they're not in Japan?<br /> <br /> This is why I kind of dislike those &quot;I mapped out the Pantheons&quot; because like... No? You put a pin in one tiny area where worship of them may have started, but it's useless TODAY because there's worshippers everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 05-15-2020, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T12:26:18-07:00","id":1388735,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11312_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11312\" data-vbnamecard=\"11312\">Maitrecorbo</a> you\u2019re not being antagonistic \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> I agree. Both are puffing. Azathoth is no more dangerous than the average Titan (very dangerous, but not automatic destruction if it wakes up).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> I guess you\u2019re huffing and puffing \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> Hmm. Maybe geographic was too narrow. But the pantheons are not all-powerful. Their influence is limited by the presence of other competing pantheons in the World.<br /> <br /> One thing I will take issue with though. Unless you\u2019re of Nordic or Germanic ancestry or you\u2019re a New Age pagan, you probably don\u2019t worship Thor in Canada.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T13:07:52-07:00","id":1388742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388735#post1388735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I will take issue with though. Unless you\u2019re of Nordic or Germanic ancestry or you\u2019re a New Age pagan, you probably don\u2019t worship Thor in Canada.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an Italian descendent, may I worship Jupiter in Brazil?<br /> <br /> Joke apart, I think the pantheons are \u201clocked\u201d in place for Fatebinding, as Fate have a greater effect on the gods than they do on Heroes. Once you have people traveling around carrying around their faiths, the gods are already binding to other places and peoples, and so, they can be worshiped by anyone they are known.<br /> <br /> Also, by our world standards, anyone worshipping Thor is a new age pagan, what allows anyone to worship Thor.<br /> <br /> Edit: before sounding offensive, Pagan is basically anyone that is not Monotheist, and new age is referring to our time, as the official worshipping of Thor was mostly lost thru the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-15-2020, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T13:53:43-07:00","id":1388752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388735#post1388735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I will take issue with though. Unless you\u2019re of Nordic or Germanic ancestry or you\u2019re a New Age pagan, you probably don\u2019t worship Thor in Canada.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would the ancestry or geographic location have any limitation on where a God goes when people pray in their names? If I, hypothetically, fully embraced Shintoism as my dedicated religion and went to a Shinto temple in America, that is, not in Japan, <i>are my prayers any less valid?</i> Would the Kami be unable to hear my voice just because the temple I'm worshipping at isn't in Japan?<br /> <br /> If I wanted to offer prayers to Durga, but I'm in Sweden, but I'm a true believer... Are my prayers unheard by Durga?<br /> <br /> Like, there are people in Canada and in the US who worship every single Pantheon in the corebook. Like, in our real world that exists today outside of the game line.<br /> <br /> Now in my games I definitely say that some Gods appear more often in certain areas than others, but that's demographics, not geography. If Thor went to Athens, he wouldn't walk right into a Theoi-only barrier that keeps Non-Theoi out. But if he made a mess in Athens, Athena may have Questions for him. In the same way you'd have questions for someone who barged into your house and ate all your food.<br /> <br /> Again, at least that's my table. But to me, region-locking Gods is something I'm really not comfortable with, as it feels like saying that someone who truly believes and practices religions outside of modernly-defined and locked geographic areas are just 'pretenders', which I don't like. Or at most charitable, dipping into the &quot;Prayer and faith powers Gods&quot; which I also don't like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T15:39:39-07:00","id":1388776,"title":"","content":"While i dont find mixing the mythos with the World pantheons to be specially interesting, i do have a friend (and potential player for a futur game) who does really like the mythos.<br /> <br /> So here is how i would use the Mythos in my games.<br /> <br /> First way (origin and hero tier) i would feature cultiat to the service of an unnamed titan. For that player i would put here and there clues with element from the Mythos that he would be able to spot.<br /> Its always fun when you, as a player, can spot threads no other player saw. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The other way (demigod tier, when its out) :<br /> I would have a group of scions betraying their divine parents/patron and working to achieve apotheosis together as a new pantheon taking &quot;mantles&quot; from the Mythos figures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T15:40:44-07:00","id":1388778,"title":"","content":"True...<br /> <br /> I\u2019m Wiccan and I\u2019m not primarily of Celtic ancestry. I guess I hadn\u2019t realized paganism was so widespread, and probably would be moreso in the World. I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> that it\u2019s more a matter of overall demographics than geography, and even that wouldn\u2019t be an absolute barrier.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T15:52:41-07:00","id":1388780,"title":"","content":"As a counterpoint of sorts, there's the fact that Godrealms connect to the World by way of special locations generally found within Terra Incognitae, like the Aesir's World Tree. While Gods aren't limited to these Axes Mundi, they do find these routes easier to traverse. And as such, they're more likely to be found near their Terra Incognitae than elsewhere. <br /> <br /> But that's not a matter of their power being restricted by geography.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T18:18:38-07:00","id":1388808,"title":"","content":"Honestly, since one is the product of the imagination of a 20th century American writer (and others who followed his,lead), and the rest are products of numerous diverse cultures and tales from around the world throughout history, it isn't surprising that the Mythos doesn't hold up against Myth for depth, detail, legend, and lore. Doesn't mean there isn't a place for it, but it isn't the same as the beliefs that are the basis of Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T11:16:57-07:00","id":1388998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388808#post1388808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, since one is the product of the imagination of a 20th century American writer (and others who followed his,lead), and the rest are products of numerous diverse cultures and tales from around the world throughout history, it isn't surprising that the Mythos doesn't hold up against Myth for depth, detail, legend, and lore. Doesn't mean there isn't a place for it, but it isn't the same as the beliefs that are the basis of Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true. Besides, the eldritch monsters of Cthulhu Mythos are supposed to be unknowable vague entities that may or may not exist. It's what driving a lovecraftian game on, the fear of the unknown. Which makes it a strange decision to try and emulate in Scion of all games for anything else than camp purposes. But oh well, if other's will find enjoyment in it then all is well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T11:25:35-07:00","id":1389003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388679#post1388679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Old Ones hated humans and were trying to spread misery, horror and destruction by their very presence in the World.<br /> <br /> In the books the Old Ones were banished or imprisoned by beings called the elder gods. Those could be the pantheons, or at least their predecessors.<br /> <br /> Just saying...</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many versions of how the Old Ones are supposed to be. The original Lovecraft versions of the Old Ones are utterly indifferent to humanity in much the same way that you are indifferent to the huge amounts of bacteria and microorganisms you kill when you wash your hands with soap.<br /> <br /> The overly antagonistic versions you are talking about who are opposed by the more or less &quot;good&quot; Elder Gods is a conceit of the author August Derleth who infused quite a lot of his Catholic world-view into the mythos. Amongst Lovecraft fans he is not well-regarded for this reason. They mean it goes against the core of nihilism and atheism that is part of cosmic horror. I'm not saying Derleth's version is &quot;incorrect&quot; or inferior, but that is a pretty common view amongst the fans of Lovecraft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 05-16-2020, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T12:52:32-07:00","id":1389045,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9849_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9849\" data-vbnamecard=\"9849\">Aristarkos</a> I didn\u2019t know any of that. I\u2019m not really a Lovecraft fan. I just think the idea of Scions fighting cosmic horrors from beyond is kinda cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T14:54:06-07:00","id":1389076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1389045#post1389045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9849_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9849\" data-vbnamecard=\"9849\">Aristarkos</a> I didn\u2019t know any of that. I\u2019m not really a Lovecraft fan. I just think the idea of Scions fighting cosmic horrors from beyond is kinda cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have my own thoughts about the book's existence, and many (including me) voiced them before, so I will not waste anyone's time saying it again, but to be honest, from my point of view, this is the best argument for the book's existence so far. It is, indeed a very cool idea.<br /> <br /> Lets all hope it is as cool, or even cooler, than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T15:10:23-07:00","id":1389082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1389045#post1389045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9849_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9849\" data-vbnamecard=\"9849\">Aristarkos</a> I didn\u2019t know any of that. I\u2019m not really a Lovecraft fan. I just think the idea of Scions fighting cosmic horrors from beyond is kinda cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, though it feels like we have that already with Scions fighting titanspawn in the core game, and many Titans (especially the Teotl ones) feel like Old Ones but with more personality and lore.<br /> <br /> Also I do not know what you are a Scion of, if it is a world without pantheons. Do you play a Scion of an Old One instead? That would seem quite gruesome...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T15:14:19-07:00","id":1389084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1389003#post1389003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are many versions of how the Old Ones are supposed to be. The original Lovecraft versions of the Old Ones are utterly indifferent to humanity in much the same way that you are indifferent to the huge amounts of bacteria and microorganisms you kill when you wash your hands with soap.<br /> <br /> The overly antagonistic versions you are talking about who are opposed by the more or less &quot;good&quot; Elder Gods is a conceit of the author August Derleth who infused quite a lot of his Catholic world-view into the mythos. Amongst Lovecraft fans he is not well-regarded for this reason. They mean it goes against the core of nihilism and atheism that is part of cosmic horror. I'm not saying Derleth's version is &quot;incorrect&quot; or inferior, but that is a pretty common view amongst the fans of Lovecraft.</div> </div> </div> </div>And speaking as someone who has no problem going on extensively about the racism threaded tightly and inseparably through Lovecraft\u2019s work - they\u2019re right. The thing that makes Cosmic Horror.... Cosmic Horror - is the idea of a cold unfeelingly alien universe in which human choice is meaningless. You turn those alien beings into forces of evil battling forces of good, and you\u2019ve defeated the entire point as now human morality defines the cosmic struggle rather than being utterly meaningless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-16-2020, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T15:15:05-07:00","id":1389085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1389082#post1389082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with this, though it feels like we have that already with Scions fighting titanspawn in the core game, and many Titans (especially the Teotl ones) feel like Old Ones but with more personality and lore.<br /> <br /> Also I do not know what you are a Scion of, if it is a world without pantheons. Do you play a Scion of an Old One instead? That would seem quite gruesome...</div> </div> </div> </div>that is something the book in question explores for the setting shard, yes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:32:52-07:00","id":1389109,"title":"","content":"A thing kd be interested in seeing in this book that i think fit certain aspect of the mythos would be mechanics and storytelling tips for dealing with Divine Revelation to mortals.<br /> A bot like that time Zeus put off the shapeshifting and showed his true form or i think the Deva also did something similar.<br /> <br /> From the mortal side of this there could be interesting elements of withstanding knowledge that mortal minds were not meant to comprehend.<br /> But theres also value in playing this from the divine side to. With how this must push the alienation of the dovine character vis a vis the mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T19:40:25-07:00","id":1389167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1389084#post1389084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And speaking as someone who has no problem going on extensively about the racism threaded tightly and inseparably through Lovecraft\u2019s work - they\u2019re right. The thing that makes Cosmic Horror.... Cosmic Horror - is the idea of a cold unfeelingly alien universe in which human choice is meaningless. You turn those alien beings into forces of evil battling forces of good, and you\u2019ve defeated the entire point as now human morality defines the cosmic struggle rather than being utterly meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course that said, there is narrative room for DECONSTRUCTING Lovecraft that isn\u2019t MISSING THE POINT of Lovecraft, but the difference there is recognizing and responding to Lovecraft\u2019s themes as opposed to just getting them wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T03:48:00-07:00","id":1394745,"title":"","content":"I recently found out that Shub-Niggurath has her own version of Satyrs, who could easily be tweaked into either a Born, or Created Scion origin.<br /> <br /> So that's already a character concept I'd be eager to try out. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","name":"NewNyrufa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T03:26:55-07:00","id":1395049,"title":"","content":"I think I wrote it before, but my approach of reconciling the Cthulhu Mythos with the setting of Scion is to assume that the Great Old Ones (though not necessarily the Outer Gods) are basically the Gods of long-lost alien civilizations. Their psychology is, of course, extremely alien - but their game rules are essentially the same, and they too are bound to Fate (hence the great focus on prophecies and the &quot;Stars becoming Right&quot;...).<br /> <br /> What makes the human pantheons different is that they still maintain a link to their old humanity... but as we know, this becomes an uphill struggle the more powerful a Scion becomes. And one day, when the last mortal human is gone - which might be soon, or it might be millenia as well - the Gods of Earth too will gradually lose their connection and be worshiped by alien beings under stranger stars - their thought processes and psychology no less disturbing to these aliens than the thoughts of Great Cthulhu is to us.<br /> <br /> So fight the Great Old Ones and their minions on Earth, by all means. You might wage titanic battles, and even win them. But in the long run, you will either remain mortal and die forgotten, or become like them.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;T<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">he time would be easy to know, for then mankind would have become as the Great Old Ones; free and wild and beyond good and evil, with laws and morals thrown aside and all men shouting and killing and revelling in joy. Then the liberated Old Ones would teach them new ways to shout and kill and revel and enjoy themselves, and all the earth would flame with a holocaust of ecstasy and freedom.</span></span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T13:58:10-07:00","id":1395140,"title":"","content":"@Jurgen Hubert, I do not care about official answer - I'm stealing your solution for the Mythos in my Scion games, from then on! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T13:59:22-07:00","id":1395141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>J\u00fcrgen Hubert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395049#post1395049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes the human pantheons different is that they still maintain a link to their old humanity... but as we know, this becomes an uphill struggle the more powerful a Scion becomes. And one day, when the last mortal human is gone - which might be soon, or it might be millenia as well - the Gods of Earth too will gradually lose their connection and be worshiped by alien beings under stranger stars - their thought processes and psychology no less disturbing to these aliens than the thoughts of Great Cthulhu is to us.[/FONT][/COLOR][/I]</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you square this with the Pantheons like the Teotl and the Deva who, when all of humanity is destroyed or dies, they can just go &quot;Welp time to go again&quot; and remake humanity again? Like, trying to go &quot;Some day humanity will die&quot; doesn't have a lot of teeth when a Deva can go &quot;Yeah, then Shiva will unmake everything and then Brahma will make humanity again, happens like clockwork&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is why I don't think the Mythos works in a setting where other Divinities exist. The moment they have to contend with the idea that their nihilistic outlook isn't the only equally true answer, they kind of get defanged. And to make them work, you gotta basically go &quot;Well maybe these other Pantheons aren't as hot as they say they are&quot; but this is never actually applied to the Lovecraftian Gods. Which is just unfair. If you're going to take the history of the Mythos at their word, you should probably do it for the OTHER Pantheons in Scion.<br /> <br /> Unless you deliberately play with the Divine Favortism via what the Companion calls the Theocentrism Dial, which is a measure of how much one Pantheon is the 'Primary' one. With the Iron setting being &quot;PCs can only be from the Favored Pantheon, with other Pantheons only being NPCs, if they exist at all&quot; and Gold being &quot;All the Pantheons are equally right, and all their myths are true&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-08-2020, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T23:30:29-07:00","id":1395252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395141#post1395141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you square this with the Pantheons like the Teotl and the Deva who, when all of humanity is destroyed or dies, they can just go &quot;Welp time to go again&quot; and remake humanity again? Like, trying to go &quot;Some day humanity will die&quot; doesn't have a lot of teeth when a Deva can go &quot;Yeah, then Shiva will unmake everything and then Brahma will make humanity again, happens like clockwork&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a given value of &quot;human&quot;. Will these really be beings that we, today, would recognize as &quot;human&quot; - with roughly the same appearance and thought modes? Or would they be starfish aliens?<br /> <br /> Also, based on what I've read on Aztec metaphysics it is <i>very</i> compatible with the Cthulhu Mythos - since everything they are doing is basically a delaying action against the inevitable dissolution of everything. <i>Nothing</i> endures forever in Aztec thought - no human, no stone, no God. Everything eventually dissolves into its primal divine force (teotl), which is then reshaped into something else entirely. And there is absolutely no guarantee that any future forms made out of teotl will be remotely human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T23:52:06-07:00","id":1395258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>J\u00fcrgen Hubert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395252#post1395252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a given value of &quot;human&quot;. Will these really be beings that we, today, would recognize as &quot;human&quot; - with roughly the same appearance and thought modes? Or would they be starfish aliens?<br /> <br /> Also, based on what I've read on Aztec metaphysics it is <i>very</i> compatible with the Cthulhu Mythos - since everything they are doing is basically a delaying action against the inevitable dissolution of everything. <i>Nothing</i> endures forever in Aztec thought - no human, no stone, no God. Everything eventually dissolves into its primal divine force (teotl), which is then reshaped into something else entirely. And there is absolutely no guarantee that any future forms made out of teotl will be remotely human.</div> </div> </div> </div>See I ask because the Teotl have explicitly had moments between when the previous suns guttered out where all humans died and they went &quot;Well time to make more humans&quot; <i>and lo they did</i> and the humans weren't giant cockroaches or fish people or sapient trees.<br /> <br /> From what I know, the only major difference has been that maybe humans of the modern age are shorter.<br /> <br /> Also, the Deva do this like clockwork, and again, the only major difference is that the humans of previous ages within the long cycle have been taller. And when the Brahma Century ends, everything gets unmade and the Trimurti will unmake and remake everything and start it all over again. And this is stated repeatedly as having happened many times within the attached myths, and is noted as it will happen again.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well how can we be sure they'll be the same this time?&quot; is a silly question when your answer is &quot;Well extrapolating out from previous data they'll be recognizably human&quot;. This is kind of what I meant by inserting the Mythos by going &quot;Well the other Myths aren't entirely truth but the Mythos? Take it as-is, it's 100% right&quot;. I shockingly don't ever see people who want to put Cthulhu in their Scion game going &quot;Well I may have to make adjustments to the Mythos in order to make it fit&quot;, they always go &quot;Yeah well maybe if we just ignore a quarter to a half of the statements of the actual religions to put them on an even playing field with the Cthulhu Mythos&quot; which is a little gross IMO.<br /> <br /> Like... Yeah, I don't want Cthulhu in the mainline because one, it doesn't work in its intended form for its intended tone. It's not HORRIFYING if they have actual competition. If anything, they give more gratitude towards the Gods that fight them, because Cthulhu and the rest are only really impressive if you're a human.<br /> <br /> The cosmic horror of the Mythos really doesn't work if there IS hope out there. If there ARE super-powered beings that do care about humans. If you remove that central concept from the Mythos, what's left? Squishy big creatures? One of whom has an octopus for a face?<br /> <br /> Granted I'm one of those types who doesn't really find cosmic-tier horror scary and considers Cthulhu basically a meme at this point and frankly finds him more than a little lame. I definitely don't think Cthulhu is on par with any of the Pantheons in the corebook. I know very little about the others in the Mythos, but what I do know I still don't find that impressive. So in a crossover, assuming you're taking all statements of the various Gods as true, the Mythos isn't that impressive. And if they're not impressive, then they lose the menace they possess with the cosmic horror angle of &quot;There are no caring Gods out there, just giant creatures that barely even notice humans and in no way care&quot;, in addition to how that level of horror loses its impact if you go &quot;Uh, Thor cares. As does Kali or Durga.&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, that's why I won't shut up about how really, the only thing that Cthulhu would add to a game with the other canon Pantheons is meme appeal and a squid face, and wouldn't actually BE the Cthulhu that captures so much fear and menace, and would just be Squid-Face the Ominous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T00:27:51-07:00","id":1395262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>J\u00fcrgen Hubert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395252#post1395252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a given value of &quot;human&quot;. Will these really be beings that we, today, would recognize as &quot;human&quot; - with roughly the same appearance and thought modes? Or would they be starfish aliens?<br /> <br /> Also, based on what I've read on Aztec metaphysics it is <i>very</i> compatible with the Cthulhu Mythos - since everything they are doing is basically a delaying action against the inevitable dissolution of everything. <i>Nothing</i> endures forever in Aztec thought - no human, no stone, no God. Everything eventually dissolves into its primal divine force (teotl), which is then reshaped into something else entirely. And there is absolutely no guarantee that any future forms made out of teotl will be remotely human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes actually... the current crop of humans in Aztec myth were made from the bones of the ones before.<br /> <br /> As for ther Deva, the humans of this age are variously said to have been descended from survivors of the last one, and we have beings who survived some apocalyspses (Hinduism has like, 4 nested Apocalypses so some people get to live through one of the inner ones but not the outermost one) who are, surprise, human.<br /> <br /> Also like, Brahma's remade humanity 17892453 times (yes, I did the Math), I think he has the general aesthetic down by now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Nothing endures in Hindu Myth either, btw... all things will die, but the Gods have a timetable for that and it will not be influenced by space calamari. Besides, it's not like the Deva are particularly lacking in multi-limbed extra-appendaged eldritch abominations who exist beyond the barriers of time and space and the sight of whose true forms rends the mind with its incomprehensibility... they just happen to think this cosmic indifference dealio is utter bullshit and are very much concerned with the lives of people. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 06-09-2020, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T03:28:04-07:00","id":1395287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395262#post1395262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes actually... the current crop of humans in Aztec myth were made from the bones of the ones before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know little about Hindu mythology, so I cannot comment on that.<br /> <br /> However, Aztec mythology also holds that the current (Fifth) Sun will be the <i>final</i> one, which will be destroyed in a cataclysm and both Earth and humanity will vanish forever. Only the divine force teotl will remain, which then expresses itself in a new form.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.iep.utm.edu/aztec\" target=\"_blank\"><i>&quot;... on earth we travel, we live along a mountain peak. Over here there is an abyss, over there there is an abyss. Wherever thou art to deviate, wherever thou art to go astray, there will thou fall, there wilt thou plunge into the deep (Sahagun 1953-82:VI,p.125).&quot;</i></a><br /> <br /> As for &quot;Devas versus Space Squids&quot;... well, what <i>happens</i> in an inter-Pantheon conflict? No idea (we will have to wait for Scion: God to come out), but in my view that's what this essentially is. The Devas might win, Great Cthulhu might win, and this is certainly important for humanity. But there are countless other worlds out there where ruins of long-ago alien civilizations are scattered across the surface, and where other Gods slumber deep in their tombs.<br /> <br /> The Gods of Earth are important to Earth, and to humanity - but they are no more &quot;special&quot; to the cosmos at large than the other Great Old Ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T03:59:31-07:00","id":1395292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>J\u00fcrgen Hubert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395287#post1395287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know little about Hindu mythology, so I cannot comment on that.<br /> <br /> However, Aztec mythology also holds that the current (Fifth) Sun will be the <i>final</i> one, which will be destroyed in a cataclysm and both Earth and humanity will vanish forever. Only the divine force teotl will remain, which then expresses itself in a new form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually commenting on your questioning why the new crops of humanity should be similar to the last ones, by pointing out that history shows that they are similar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>J\u00fcrgen Hubert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395287#post1395287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for &quot;Devas versus Space Squids&quot;... well, what <i>happens</i> in an inter-Pantheon conflict? No idea (we will have to wait for Scion: God to come out), but in my view that's what this essentially is. The Devas might win, Great Cthulhu might win, and this is certainly important for humanity. But there are countless other worlds out there where ruins of long-ago alien civilizations are scattered across the surface, and where other Gods slumber deep in their tombs.<br /> <br /> The Gods of Earth are important to Earth, and to humanity - but they are no more &quot;special&quot; to the cosmos at large than the other Great Old Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong... the Gods of Earth are important to the Cosmos because they created the Cosmos. The Deva have created multiple Universes of which our perceptible part is only two layers of fourteen... the Theoi knows the stars very well; after all, they created most of them, out of lovers and loyal servants or hubristic humans to serve as a warning... the God of Abraham created all the Heavens and the Earth, not just the sky above our planet... The Teotl are not going down without a fight, and what need they fear demons from the stars? They've been dealing with them since the Fifth Sun rose.<br /> <br /> The Mediocre Old Ones might be Gods of distant civilizations, but if we are to accept their Cosmology as True, it stands to reason that the same Cosmos is the domain of the Pantheons of Earth... They are fundamental to the Cosmos at large, because that is what their Cosmology says they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T05:00:46-07:00","id":1395304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>J\u00fcrgen Hubert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395287#post1395287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know little about Hindu mythology, so I cannot comment on that.<br /> <br /> However, Aztec mythology also holds that the current (Fifth) Sun will be the <i>final</i> one, which will be destroyed in a cataclysm and both Earth and humanity will vanish forever. Only the divine force teotl will remain, which then expresses itself in a new form.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.iep.utm.edu/aztec\" target=\"_blank\"><i>&quot;... on earth we travel, we live along a mountain peak. Over here there is an abyss, over there there is an abyss. Wherever thou art to deviate, wherever thou art to go astray, there will thou fall, there wilt thou plunge into the deep (Sahagun 1953-82:VI,p.125).&quot;</i></a><br /> <br /> As for &quot;Devas versus Space Squids&quot;... well, what <i>happens</i> in an inter-Pantheon conflict? No idea (we will have to wait for Scion: God to come out), but in my view that's what this essentially is. The Devas might win, Great Cthulhu might win, and this is certainly important for humanity. But there are countless other worlds out there where ruins of long-ago alien civilizations are scattered across the surface, and where other Gods slumber deep in their tombs.<br /> <br /> The Gods of Earth are important to Earth, and to humanity - but they are no more &quot;special&quot; to the cosmos at large than the other Great Old Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as a caveat, you are completely misinterpreting that Sahag\u00fan quote. It's not intended to signify a coming cataclysm in the interpretation offered by the site you linked either. This quote is about how easy it is to fall into sin and thus ruin, not about how precarious the continued existence of the world itself is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T05:30:22-07:00","id":1395316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>J\u00fcrgen Hubert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395287#post1395287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gods of Earth are important to Earth, and to humanity - but they are no more &quot;special&quot; to the cosmos at large than the other Great Old Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Jurgen</b>, you maybe too low in your <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392721#post1392721\">Theocentrism compared to mainstream <b>Scion</b> setting and forum </a>- you describe world on Bronze or maybe even Iron Theocentrism, where mainstream <b>Scion </b>is on <b><u>Gold</u></b> level of this Dial. I agree with you on general - especially <u>loving</u> takes on 'Earth's vs Cosmos Gods' - just I mark that official stuff for gameline mark that 'Every Myth is True' - so Pantheons <i>really</i> created universe as whole. / Even if it's MEGA logical-reality conflicts between them. /<br /> <br /> Here is more from <b>Scion: Companion</b> preview blog ( from over 1,5 years ago ) on Myth Levels / Dials:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myth Levels preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>CHAPTER ONE: MYTH LEVEL</b><br /> <br /> The Myth Level is five options along four axes of design, meant to allow the Storyguide to choose how many of Scion\u2019s setting \u201cdials\u201d they want to crank. This chapter lays out what each of those dials looks like at each of the five Myth Levels. Those Myth Levels are:<ul><li><b>Iron:</b> Perfectly mundane. Very similar in nature and tone to Gaiman\u2019s <b><i>American Gods</i></b>, where ifriti are cab drivers, Odhinn is a shiftless wandering con man, and Chernobog and the goddesses of dawn, midday and evening are poor immigrants scraping by in a shitty apartment in Chicago.</li> <li><b>Heroic: </b>Mostly mundane, but with room for great acts of heroism. Most supernatural creatures still have mundane manifestations here (that centaur is still just a biker here), but Scions and gods may appear as impressive and tremendous \u2013 Aphrodite isn\u2019t some burnt out barfly here, she\u2019s drop-dead gorgeous and probably on fashion covers. This is the level of the <b><i>Iliad</i> </b>and the <i><b>Odyssey</b></i>.</li> <li><b>Bronze: </b>This is where the supernatural really comes into play. Creatures of Legend shed their mundane disguises in areas of Bronze Myth, and appear in their true nature. Magic becomes overt here, and Demigods wield their true power. This is <b><i>Clash of the Titans</i></b> territory, and there might just actually be dragons in that undetailed area of the map.</li> <li><b>Silver: </b>Past the threshold of urban myth and getting into epic fantasy, places of Silver Myth are deeply resonant with Myth. They are often fanciful places and hidden vales of magic technically found in the World, but not of it. The power of a creature of Legend is reflected in its appearance \u2013 the mightier the entity, the more impressive it appears. Zelazny\u2019s <i><b>Lord of Light</b> </i>goes into this area of Myth in its narrative.</li> <li><b>Gold:</b> Flat-out mythological, where symbolism is the same as its reality. Places of Gold Myth are not even of this World. Lots of <b>Scion</b> 1e went into this territory, with its otherworldly locales, and lots of fantasy that touches on extradimensional areas and the like qualify.</li> </ul>The trick is this: you should be able to choose a starting Myth Level and then turn each dial up or down within that level to taste. So, for instance, as Storyguide I might choose to start at the Iron Level but crank the Titanomachy up, turning <b><i>American Gods</i></b> into a raging shadow war that you have to keep peeling back layers of the World to see.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392781#post1392781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example the standard setting for the World is.<br /> Genre : Bronze<br /> Theocentrism : Gold<br /> Titanomachy : Silver<br /> Evidence : Silver</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-09-2020, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T05:58:56-07:00","id":1395322,"title":"","content":"I sadly do not have the Companion, but nothing at this scale - not even Gold - strikes me as fundamentally incompatible with the Cthulhu Mythos, which has grand and terrible vistas all of its own.<br /> <br /> What I would emphasize for my vision is the fundamental Trans- and Posthumanism of Scion. At the lower tiers, Scions are still fundamentally human - but if they embrace their heritage and walk on the path to Godhood, they will shed more and more of their humanity until they become Gods - which are, fundamentally, the same class of beings as many of the Great Old Ones. Obviously, they maintain a stronger connection to humanity than the existing Great Old Ones (who evolved on alien worlds under stranger skies)... but in the end, they are not that different.<br /> <br /> And that's how I would make Lovecraftian Cosmic Horror work for Scion. The younger, more recently evolved Gods still have recognizable human motivations - but this will wane as time goes on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T06:25:00-07:00","id":1395328,"title":"","content":"This discussion is not actually about reconciling the Mythos of H. P. Lovecraft's paracosm with the beliefs and myths of various cultures around the world, it is a discussion about <i>primacy</i>. Fundamentally, this is an issue that shows up just as much when merging two pieces of fiction in a crossover fanfiction - which makes sense because P&amp;P Roleplay is basically extended cooperative fanfiction with a conflict resolution mechanism - as it does now when we discuss this matter. Painting with a broad brush, it is not possible to ever reconcile two propositions that make contrary claims without giving primacy to one claim over another. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10279\" data-vbnamecard=\"10279\">J\u00fcrgen Hubert</a> claims to have reconciled them, but this is only true insofar as he has implicitly given one of them primacy over the other, just like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> have <i>explicitly</i> given the claims of divinities primacy over that of the Mythos.<br /> <br /> What I mean by this is that Scion's default statement is loosely that all myths are true and that it is simply a matter of from which 'layer' one happens to view the world. In one layer, the goddess sang of the rage of the Pele\u00efd Akhilleus and the countless ills he brought upon the Akhaians, in another layer the same is at most a post-hoc legendary figure whose legend became paramount in the Greek Dark Ages when the scattered chiefdoms of post-Mykenaian Greece looked back on a past they no longer remembered but in a haze and told stories of the great cyclopean walls and constructions left from those times. In this sense, Scion very carefully avoids giving any story primacy over others because what Scion deals with is not two (or eight or twelve) pieces of fiction to be reconciled, but the very real beliefs and traditions of real human beings, some of which have lived for a long time in a situation in which the primacy has been given to whoever happened to rule over them at the time. Whether these are the Parsi of India who had to explain our Mazdayasna in terms of angels and archangels or face persecution from the Church of Scotland or the Nahua of Mexico who became heathens in the minds of Spanish <i>conquistadores</i> who imagined the frontiers of the <i>Virreinato de Nueva Espa\u00f1a</i> as a new <i>reconquista </i>and the lands of the former Triple Alliance as a new Emirate of Granada does not really matter. A &quot;reconciliation&quot; of the Mythos of H. P. Lovecraft with the beliefs most mythologies in the world that states that the deities of the Mythos are simply the gods of older beings, strange and alien to nascent humanity, who once lived in foreign vistas amidst the stars before themselves being extinguished by the passage of time is not a compromise between them at all. It is an all but explicit statement that the gods are either wrong or lying, that they did not create the world or matter much beyond a simple lonely orb of land and water passing through the universe, the universe is fundamentally Darwinian and gods evolve and die as time passes and the universe did not have its origin in anything but a concentration of meaningless particles.<br /> <br /> You can run a game built on such a premise and it could even work for certain pantheons, but if you were to tell me - a Zoroastrian - that it is <i>fully compatible</i> with the Mythos to have the world be created not by Ahura Mazda but through complete randomness and to have the <i>actual</i> truth of the world be one of meaninglessness and purposelessness rather than that of the threefold path of Asha and that gods are simply powerful beings and nothing more, I would certainly raise my eyebrow in confusion. It is valid and fine to choose to prioritize the atmosphere of cosmic horror and make changes based on that, but you have to acknowledge and accept that it <i>requires</i> making changes and I hope that you can certainly understand why many of us people of faith are little inclined to make changes to something that matters quite deeply to us in order to prioritize the vision of a New English guy from the 20th century who would with most likelihood despise us if we stood in front of him, flesh and blood.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This came out a bit more aggressive than I'd have wanted to (and also I spelled a name wrong), so I do want to clarify that I like the works of Lovecraft even though I know he would most probably find me an abomination against God that weakens the blood of the white race. I also do not mean to imply any hard feelings for choosing to prioritize the feeling of cosmic horror and the Mythos for the sake of the game, I just wanted to make it clear that there<i> was a choice being made</i> and that this was not simply a matter of reconciling but of picking and choosing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":6042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","user":"ManusDomine","date":".  Fixed a name and added a comment. 06-09-2020, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T06:42:20-07:00","id":1395334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1388679#post1388679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a> I hate that conceit!!! Literally gives me a headache trying to figure it out. If I ever ran Scion, my version would be \u201cThe World exists independently of the pantheons. They may SAY they created the world, but they didn\u2019t. Everything else is (mostly) true, but only in that pantheon\u2019s geographic area of influence.\u201d<br /> <br /> Again, I don\u2019t take those claims literally. \u201cGuarantees victory against any foe\u201d is just Tuatha puffing (means exaggerated claims in advertising).</div> </div> </div> </div>Side topic - I advise <b>Scion Companion</b> to you, <b>Penelope</b>. You seem, as I'm, to prefer Bronze or even Heroic Theocentrism - where claims of Pantheons are not whole truth and 'All Myths are True' is resolved by 'Oh, they SAY that - and the gods have real magic - but Earth still has 4.54 billion years and dinosaurs where real before - just like evolution'. I may start topic on general Theocentrism Dial in <b>Scion </b>2E settings - and it's repercussions.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Started separate topic on discussion of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1395335-companion-theocentrism-evidance-dials\">Theocentrism &amp; Evidance Dials for the game World</a></b>. Will be probably interested in it, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> and @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j%C3%BCrgen-hubert\">J\u00fcrgen</a></b> . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-09-2020, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T07:19:17-07:00","id":1395340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395334#post1395334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Side topic - I advise <b>Scion Companion</b> to you, <b>Penelope</b>. You seem, as I'm, to prefer Bronze or even Heroic Theocentrism - where claims of Pantheons are not whole truth and 'All Myths are True' is resolved by 'Oh, they SAY that - and the gods have real magic - but Earth still has 4543E9 years and dinosaurs where real before - just like evolution'. I may start topic on general Theocentrism Dial in <b>Scion </b>2E settings - and it's repercussions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Demon the Fallen I have an issue with the idea of multiple Layers of reality that intersect. I know it\u2019s not the case for Scion, but it sounds like a escuse for something that were not planned from the beginning (like old WoD). In Scion, it\u2019s not the case, but it makes it really hard to design a story focusing in a myth, just because it is true but also not at all.<br /> <br /> I prefers to work on a Iron/Heroic Theocentrism running around a shared past that is denied by the gods old enough to be alive back then, maybe because of their Legend, maybe because of Fate, maybe just to deny their past as Scions themselves. Sorry for those that have their religion denied partially, but it\u2019s hard to force everything in the same box and have a reasonable way to work.<br /> <br /> In this case, Jurgen Hubert point of view is the best way to play The Old Ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T09:31:56-07:00","id":1395373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395340#post1395340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefers to work on a Iron/Heroic Theocentrism running around a shared past that is denied by the gods old enough to be alive back then, maybe because of their Legend, maybe because of Fate, maybe just to deny their past as Scions themselves. Sorry for those that have their religion denied partially, but it\u2019s hard to force everything in the same box and have a reasonable way to work.<br /> <br /> In this case, Jurgen Hubert point of view is the best way to play The Old Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>So by this logic, the 'Eternal Alien Mythos' only say they're eternal and alien, right? Because Lovecraft's books are less than a century old. Clearly, if we're pulling the 'Well the Religions are only as old as we have recordings of them' then we have to pull it for Lovecraft's works as well. Again, <i>why do they get the benefit of the doubt here</i>?<br /> <br /> Also, to clarify, I'm not going to say that Old Religions are more 'correct' than modern ones. A religion that's less than a century old in our history should be just as True as the tales of the Mesopotamian Gods. Like, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza\" target=\"_blank\">the Cortes Divinas</a> for example are a relatively young religion, but I love them and would be happy to include them in any of my games.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying it strikes me as VERY hypocritical to go &quot;Okay religions that people believed in and still do believe in, I know your stories say that your Gods have been around THIS long, but we're not gonna take you at your word&quot; and then turn around and go &quot;Right, not-religion of Space Squids that was written down less than a century ago: You say that you're eternal and lived long before our world was formed from space dust? Seems legit, I believe you, I can buy that you're as old as you say you are and you only told someone about this at this point&quot;<br /> <br /> The whole &quot;Sorry for those that have their religions denied partially&quot; rings particularly hollow when it's followed up by not taking similar liberties to let Cthulhu play in the same sandbox and just assuming everything that happens in the Mythos is true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-09-2020, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T10:24:32-07:00","id":1395390,"title":"","content":"It's kind of funny in context, given Lovecraft explicitly always wrote with deeply unreliable narrators so everything that is assumed here is basically conclusions taken from the ravings of madmen and people who had no idea of what they were doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T11:03:00-07:00","id":1395400,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t mean the gods are as old as the religions, let me explain my Scion head cannon for an iron/heroic campaign:<br /> <br /> The gods existed for a long time, the primordials may be as old as the universe, and the titans and gods my be much older than humanity, but it doesn\u2019t mean all their stories are history. I will use the pantheon I am more familiar with.<br /> <br /> Gaia is as old as Earth, is one of the multiple aspects (mantles, maybe) of the spirit of Earth (the planet, not the element), all the other primordials came from Earth, as they are locals. They don\u2019t look human, because they are gods, but they choose to look human to interact with humans. The true forms of the gods may turn people crazy (or dead)<br /> Zeus dethroned Kronos? Yes. Titanomachia happened before humans raise, and the Gigantomachia happened after (taking a long time actually, several generations of heroes fought in it).<br /> The Sun is Apollo chariot? no, the Sun is a humongous ball of fire at millions of kilometers from Earth. Apollo chariot is a big and bright chariot pulled by ferocious and hard to thane fire horses, but not the sun.<br /> <br /> There are other dimensions, the various underworlds are some of them, as well as the gods realms and other Terra incognita (the other non divine worlds of Yggdrasil, for example).<br /> <br /> The Lovecraftian gods are gods that possibly survived the destruction or were exiled from their planets a long time ago, some departed with their worshipers, others alone, but most of them just don\u2019t care about mortals anymore.<br /> <br /> The same way Earth has its own spirit and several aspects, the universe has its own aspects, but, it usually don\u2019t care much about any of the quintillion cultures around the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T13:09:06-07:00","id":1395444,"title":"","content":"I admit that when I crack open a book about playing Myths and Gods and Heroes, my first thought is not in fact &quot;Well gonna scribble out half the religions and cosmology rules&quot;. Like, I plan to embrace the madness and go whole hog on the kind of Silliness that playing with the Divine allows.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Sun's a miasma of incandescent plasma, and a shiny barge, and at least two chariots driven by different people. What does it appear as if you launch yourself into space? Well, that depends on what you're looking for, what you expect, whether you're a Scion or not...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T15:12:22-07:00","id":1395462,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that Scion 2e operates by rules somewhat akin to <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>: when a group of Gods get together and found a new Pantheon, <i>reality itself gets rewritten</i> so that that Pantheon's Myths are True and have always been True. That said, unless you have a time machine (which isn't really something that <b>Scion</b> deals with), that latter bit is mostly a moot point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T15:25:40-07:00","id":1395466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395462#post1395462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that Scion 2e operates by rules somewhat akin to <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>: when a group of Gods get together and found a new Pantheon, <i>reality itself gets rewritten</i> so that that Pantheon's Myths are True and have always been True. That said, unless you have a time machine (which isn't really something that <b>Scion</b> deals with), that latter bit is mostly a moot point.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I understand, and so it\u2019s possible to presume a Hero can creat a cult, that increase the legend and become a religion, turning him into a god that retroactively created the world they were born. That\u2019s Legen... wait for it... dary! Legendary!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T16:14:00-07:00","id":1395477,"title":"","content":"Note, I said a group of gods. I suspect that this is beyond the ability of an individual god to do on his or her own \u2014 though becoming a Primordial might let you do it all by yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T17:40:58-07:00","id":1395487,"title":"","content":"I think to a degree, Gods also have the ability to fuck with their own backstory even if they're achieve Apotheosis without forming a new Pantheon. Like Athena probably started out as a Hero when she burst from Zeus's head, but upon achieving Apotheosis was able to go back and say &quot;No, I was always a Goddess, from day one!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T17:43:54-07:00","id":1395488,"title":"","content":"Athena is an example of several Gods sharing the same Mantle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T18:14:07-07:00","id":1395494,"title":"","content":"See, you agree with me on the part \u201cgods tell their legends\u201d and they become true. The only thing we disagree is that I don\u2019t think it becomes history, just becomes kind of true.<br /> <br /> Basically a god of sun can make it looks like he is or is riding / surfing / sailing / rowing the sun, but the sun is still the sun, they can even use their power to make it darker or whatever in a large portion of the world or in a terra incognita just to show he is the true sun, but in the end it\u2019s just an extension of his power.<br /> <br /> Look, I don\u2019t want to change your way to play, I just want to show the way I think fit on the game if you make it Iron/Heroic And keep all the pantheons with their own myths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T22:24:00-07:00","id":1395527,"title":"","content":"If it becomes true, doesn't it become history? Like, if Surya is the Sun, and always has been the Sun, and that has become True with Surya's Legend... Then hasn't that become history, because it's true and always has been true?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T04:17:32-07:00","id":1395576,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s not true on a more Iron/Heroic, while may be in a Bronze+. That\u2019s basically the way Theocentrism works, as I see, the higher Theocentrism the more true the myths are, high while on lower Theocentrism it is not true at all (even the gods being true).<br /> <br /> In a gold Theocentrism setting, when Athena become god, if the legend says she has always been a god and was born from the head of Zeus, she never had a lower legend and nobody (including gods, and even Athena) will remember her as a Hero, always as a god. In a lower Theocentrism setting, people will know the story but anyone that lived during Athena ascension will remember her as a hero/demigod yet she may have being born from Zeus head, and in a Iron setting it\u2019s only a story they tell so Athena was never young and silly as all the kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T04:40:49-07:00","id":1395578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1395576#post1395576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not true on a more Iron/Heroic, while may be in a Bronze+. That\u2019s basically the way Theocentrism works, as I see, the higher Theocentrism the more true the myths are, high while on lower Theocentrism it is not true at all (even the gods being true).<br /> <br /> In a gold Theocentrism setting, when Athena become god, if the legend says she has always been a god and was born from the head of Zeus, she never had a lower legend and nobody (including gods, and even Athena) will remember her as a Hero, always as a god. In a lower Theocentrism setting, people will know the story but anyone that lived during Athena ascension will remember her as a hero/demigod yet she may have being born from Zeus head, and in a Iron setting it\u2019s only a story they tell so Athena was never young and silly as all the kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not what Theocentrism means. Theocentrism is a measure of how 'Central' a particular Pantheon is to the World. Iron Theocentrism does *not* mean that no myths are true... it means that the Myths of only one Pantheon are True... thus, if said Pantheon were the Greek, Athena absolutely *would* have always been a God. If you choose a setting with No Pantheons, then there are *no* Gods, rather than false ones, and the PCs are limited to pre-Visitation Scions and Denizens, not Heroes.<br /> <br /> You don't get to have your cake and eat it too... Either gods are *Gods*, in which case they have Scions and are the Truth of the World... or they don't even really exist and you don't have Heroes... this 'Gods are just powerful Wizards' style setting is completely at odds with the genre of Scion, which is ultimately Myth, and continually strikes me as trying to do a vampire setting that has no blood or life drinking... what even are you looking for in a vampire game then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 06-10-2020, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T15:00:40-07:00","id":1398881,"title":"","content":"Here's my two cents on how to incorporate the Mythos into a regular Scion world. How I'd run it is that the World is like a conglomeration of bubbles somehow layered on top and within each other and generally allow for the others existences. The Mythos bubble is different. It's on the outside and it doesn't want to be integrated with the other pantheons. The Mythos deities don't really want to be fatebound to the Earth but they can't cause too much trouble or the bubbles will pop. The Earth Gods want the bubbles to be intact to prevent the Mythos deities from adding to the Titan problem and the Mythos want to avoid cross-contaminating with the Earth any more than necessary. Because in the original stories the Earth is just another rock in space to them. In Scion the Earth very important and it is aggravating for the Mythos deities to be bound to just a simple rock.<br /> <br /> For a campaign this means that Heroes would mostly be dealing with anything that was summoned or slipped across the barrier between the bubbles. Demi-gods and Gods would deal with bigger threats but also would want to ensure the barrier between the bubbles don't get too unstable. Cause while some of the more powerful gods wouldn't have too much trouble against the Mythos deities not every god is all powerful. Not to mention the collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Edit: you can even add in the idea that the Earth Gods are as strange and incomprehensible to the Mythos deities as the Mythos is to regular humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26256-curiosity","user":"Curiosity","date":". 06-25-2020, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26256-curiosity","name":"Curiosity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T18:30:25-07:00","id":1398914,"title":"","content":"I admit i'm endlessly curious why people want to put Cthulhu in Mainline Scion.<br /> <br /> Like the very main themes, arguably the entire point that makes Cthulhu more than just a big squidface, is the cosmic horror angle of a cole indifferent vast universe that humanity ultimately doesn't matter to. There are beings far greater than us, and they barely realize we exist.<br /> <br /> The thing is, this vanishes the moment you mix in other Gods who do exist and who do care about humanity for the most part. And if you remove that central point from Cthulhu... Why bother? Is it Cthulhu if you remove the very point of the Mythos? Or is it just Ol Jimmy Squidface?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T19:04:16-07:00","id":1398919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1398914#post1398914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit i'm endlessly curious why people want to put Cthulhu in Mainline Scion.<br /> <br /> Like the very main themes, arguably the entire point that makes Cthulhu more than just a big squidface, is the cosmic horror angle of a cole indifferent vast universe that humanity ultimately doesn't matter to. There are beings far greater than us, and they barely realize we exist.<br /> <br /> The thing is, this vanishes the moment you mix in other Gods who do exist and who do care about humanity for the most part. And if you remove that central point from Cthulhu... Why bother? Is it Cthulhu if you remove the very point of the Mythos? Or is it just Ol Jimmy Squidface?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That assumes that it's the Cthulhu Mythos is the right way to speak of Lovecraft's tales. I'm with those who prefer to think of Lovecraft's stories as the Yog-sothoth mythos. Remember that the Dreamlands in &quot;Dreamquest for Unknown Kadath&quot; contain the Gods, the Dead, the Demons, and others. The Gods of Earth are pretty much captives, if honored ones, of Nyarlathotep. Struggle between Nyarlathotep, a monstrously selfish being desiring to eliminate Fate by eliminating mankind,, and the Gods, would be very different than Lovecraft's tales, Still, given the trouble a mere human dreamer like Randolph Carter causes him, Nyarlathotep has reason to loathe humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T19:57:47-07:00","id":1398932,"title":"","content":"I'm pondering the feasibility of taking regular Origin Scion and trying to make it CoC like by adjusting the dials. Genre at Iron or low Heroic, Titanomachy at Silver or Gold, Evidence at Iron and Theocentricism at maybe Bronze or Silver, so you have a lot of horrible monsters in the shadows but the gods cant or wont do much about it, leaving only a brave handful of mortal(ish) investigators to do anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T20:04:54-07:00","id":1398935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1398919#post1398919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That assumes that it's the Cthulhu Mythos is the right way to speak of Lovecraft's tales. I'm with those who prefer to think of Lovecraft's stories as the Yog-sothoth mythos. Remember that the Dreamlands in &quot;Dreamquest for Unknown Kadath&quot; contain the Gods, the Dead, the Demons, and others. The Gods of Earth are pretty much captives, if honored ones, of Nyarlathotep. Struggle between Nyarlathotep, a monstrously selfish being desiring to eliminate Fate by eliminating mankind,, and the Gods, would be very different than Lovecraft's tales, Still, given the trouble a mere human dreamer like Randolph Carter causes him, Nyarlathotep has reason to loathe humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I'm unfamiliar with this story but I gotta ask how you imprison ALL the other Gods of Humanity?<br /> <br /> Scratch that: How do you do that without the explanation of &quot;The Author thinks Gods are chumps and wants to really sell how serious these Elder Gods are&quot;?<br /> <br /> Also, why can a being literally contain ALL THE GODS but is undone by one human dreamer? Is this some kind of &quot;Humanity's potential is greater than the Gods&quot; message?<br /> <br /> And now we're back to the upthread assumption of &quot;We take the stated powers of these (demonstrably imagined) Gods as true, but we nerf and kneecap the OTHER Gods to make the Lovecraft Beings a serious threat&quot; which will never taste right to me. Like, how can Nyarlathotep contain the Deva, who are effectively everything?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T20:35:19-07:00","id":1398939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1398914#post1398914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit i'm endlessly curious why people want to put Cthulhu in Mainline Scion.<br /> <br /> Like the very main themes, arguably the entire point that makes Cthulhu more than just a big squidface, is the cosmic horror angle of a cole indifferent vast universe that humanity ultimately doesn't matter to. There are beings far greater than us, and they barely realize we exist.<br /> <br /> The thing is, this vanishes the moment you mix in other Gods who do exist and who do care about humanity for the most part. And if you remove that central point from Cthulhu... Why bother? Is it Cthulhu if you remove the very point of the Mythos? Or is it just Ol Jimmy Squidface?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now I'm going to admit that I'm more familiar with Cthulhu Mythos deities than I am with the Deva so please bear that in mind. <br /> <br /> For me the Mythos is less about the absolute lack of caring gods in existence and the utter nihilism of Earth's place in the universe and more about the absolute strangeness and disconnect the Great Old ones and the Elder Gods have with what humanity knows about reality. Bast and Nodens/Nuada are actually considered a part of the Mythos, not sure when they were added but I know they were at some point, and are generally seen as having some interest in Earth's continued existence. How much they care depends on the writer.<br /> <br /> Now to me the whole point of the Mythos is that the closer you get to them the further you get from your previous understanding of reality. Take for example the Color Out of Space. It is a story where a meteor crashes onto a farm and an entity contained within poisons the well and leeches the life out of everything in the area. The horror is found in how strange this entity seemingly made entirely of light came from somewhere so far beyond the laws of physics that the light itself is a color never seen on Earth, which science says is impossible. So I'd say that rather than dismissing the power of the Earth Gods you focus on how incompatible the Mythos deities are. How one investigating them might become lost to almost everything, even death itself. And not in the escape from reincarnation Hindu way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26256-curiosity","name":"Curiosity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T21:49:48-07:00","id":1398944,"title":"","content":"different perspective:<br /> The &quot;Elder gods&quot; are just a band of scions from the 1930's/40's, who saw that their divine parents didn't care about the world, so they decided to see how powerful they could get.<br /> All of them ended up going down the &quot;horrifying&quot; divine appearance, and are intently trying to convince people they're more powerful than the other gods, and older than the universe etc etc.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft and the authors who followed him are just the leading edge of the propoganda machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23957-atlassniperman","name":"AtlasSniperman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T07:15:17-07:00","id":1399058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtlasSniperman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1398944#post1398944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">different perspective:<br /> The &quot;Elder gods&quot; are just a band of scions from the 1930's/40's, who saw that their divine parents didn't care about the world, so they decided to see how powerful they could get.<br /> All of them ended up going down the &quot;horrifying&quot; divine appearance, and are intently trying to convince people they're more powerful than the other gods, and older than the universe etc etc.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft and the authors who followed him are just the leading edge of the propoganda machine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This must be the best one I've seen so far. If I would in some way, shape or form integrate the Mythos to Mainline I'd love to make them lame edgy wannabe gods of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T11:37:31-07:00","id":1399103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Curiosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1398939#post1398939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bast and Nodens/Nuada are actually considered a part of the Mythos, not sure when they were added but I know they were at some point, and are generally seen as having some interest in Earth's continued existence. How much they care depends on the writer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine they were added much the same way that Dagon was 'added' to the Mythos, in that the writer just took the name of a God and said &quot;They're part of this too&quot; and not having a lot of connection with the actual deity.<br /> <br /> If that came up at my table I'd probably flat-out say &quot;They have the same name, but they're not THOSE Bast and Nuada&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Though I've no real objection to Atlas's take on &quot;These identities were assumed by other Scions who achieved Apotheosis&quot;, save for my basic objection of finding the Lovecraft Entities really boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-26-2020, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T17:57:32-07:00","id":1399176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1399103#post1399103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine they were added much the same way that Dagon was 'added' to the Mythos, in that the writer just took the name of a God and said &quot;They're part of this too&quot; and not having a lot of connection with the actual deity.<br /> <br /> If that came up at my table I'd probably flat-out say &quot;They have the same name, but they're not THOSE Bast and Nuada&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Though I've no real objection to Atlas's take on &quot;These identities were assumed by other Scions who achieved Apotheosis&quot;, save for my basic objection of finding the Lovecraft Entities really boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nodens is in stories by HPL as is Bast. Both are in multiple editions of Chaosium's Call of Cthulhu. As Lovecraft adored cats, Bast was a shooin. Nodens, whose worship was accepted and respected by the Romans, was a respectable British god in HPL's anglophile eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-26-2020, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T08:57:12-07:00","id":1399299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1399176#post1399176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nodens is in stories by HPL as is Bast. Both are in multiple editions of Chaosium's Call of Cthulhu. As Lovecraft adored cats, Bast was a shooin. Nodens, whose worship was accepted and respected by the Romans, was a respectable British god in HPL's anglophile eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Lovecraft threw them in and probably in ways that would make the Gods in question go &quot;Wait what?&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, bout what I though. I'll stick with my stance of &quot;They have the same names but they're not the same Gods&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T09:59:10-07:00","id":1399309,"title":"","content":"I would make them crazy mantles of the respective gods. I don\u2019t know how the gods can switch mantles, but if they work as multiple personalities, they could be a mechanism of defense against the alien minds or something similar.<br /> <br /> Nodens, if I my memory don\u2019t fail, is a hunter of old ones, with those weird hounds working for him. It sounds like a god that went crazy on revenge or just to show how powerful he is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 06-27-2020, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T11:28:15-07:00","id":1399326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1399103#post1399103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine they were added much the same way that Dagon was 'added' to the Mythos, in that the writer just took the name of a God and said &amp;quot;They're part of this too&amp;quot; and not having a lot of connection with the actual deity.<br /> <br /> If that came up at my table I'd probably flat-out say &amp;quot;They have the same name, but they're not THOSE Bast and Nuada&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Though I've no real objection to Atlas's take on &amp;quot;These identities were assumed by other Scions who achieved Apotheosis&amp;quot;, save for my basic objection of finding the Lovecraft Entities really boring.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23957-atlassniperman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23957\" data-vbnamecard=\"23957\">AtlasSniperman</a> about the Mantles and identities of the Elder Gods, but I don\u2019t agree that the Cthulhu Mythos is \u201creally boring.\u201d I would love to see a more direct crossover between \u201cregular\u201d Scion and Masks of the Mythos (a world in which the pantheons and the Mythos exist in the same universe and possibly compete for worshippers).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also REALLY looking forward to Mysteries of the World coming out on DTRPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T11:30:21-07:00","id":1399328,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz is \u201ccrazy mantle\u201d an actual gaming term or are you just using it as an adjective like as in \u201cShe\u2019s crazy hot?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T12:03:06-07:00","id":1399345,"title":"","content":"Crazy more like Insane... definitely not a gaming term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T14:35:49-07:00","id":1399387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1399326#post1399326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23957-atlassniperman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23957\" data-vbnamecard=\"23957\">AtlasSniperman</a> about the Mantles and identities of the Elder Gods, but I don\u2019t agree that the Cthulhu Mythos is \u201creally boring.\u201d I would love to see a more direct crossover between \u201cregular\u201d Scion and Masks of the Mythos (a world in which the pantheons and the Mythos exist in the same universe and possibly compete for worshippers).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also REALLY looking forward to Mysteries of the World coming out on DTRPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>... I mean like, what's there to compete with?<br /> <br /> On one hand you have the Theoi or the Teotl or the Deva who keep the world running, bless their champions, ensure the proper way of things, may give you an afterlife...<br /> <br /> On the OTHER hand you have the Lovecraft Gods, who are big, scary, and at best see you as insects beneath their notice or at worst actively hate you.<br /> <br /> <i>Who would worship the Outer Gods?</i> These guys fucking suck from the perspective of a mortal. Like, how would that pitch meeting go between worshippers?<br /> <br /> Theoi Worshipper: Zeus guarantees law and order and ensures oaths are kept.<br /> <br /> Teotl Worshipper: Our gods give of their blood and flesh to provide water and food and keep the sun ablaze. They ask for offerings, yes, but they do not ask for that which they are not willing to give. It's a divine pact.<br /> <br /> Deva Worshipper: So I danced for the entire day until my feet were numb but after Kali blessed me and helped my partner and I have a child together, it's a literal miracle!<br /> <br /> Mythos Worshipper: My God actively hates me and the only benefit I get from this is that when they try to kill everyone I'll get eaten first. Or ignored.<br /> <br /> Anunna Worshipper: Bruh my pantheon only recently started calling humanity their subjects instead of their slaves and <i>I</i> think that you gotta get out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T15:19:43-07:00","id":1399406,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> OMG \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> Okay you made your point \ud83d\ude0a. But that still doesn\u2019t mean the Mythos and their worshippers can\u2019t exist as antagonists in the same universe as Scions of the pantheons. Or what about a Begotten Scion of Yog-Sothoth who is just now realizing how bad her divine parent sucks and needs the Band\u2019s help in stopping the rise of the Mythos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T16:51:53-07:00","id":1399428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1399387#post1399387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... I mean like, what's there to compete with?<br /> <br /> On one hand you have the Theoi or the Teotl or the Deva who keep the world running, bless their champions, ensure the proper way of things, may give you an afterlife...<br /> <br /> On the OTHER hand you have the Lovecraft Gods, who are big, scary, and at best see you as insects beneath their notice or at worst actively hate you.<br /> <br /> <i>Who would worship the Outer Gods?</i> These guys fucking suck from the perspective of a mortal. Like, how would that pitch meeting go between worshippers?<br /> <br /> Theoi Worshipper: Zeus guarantees law and order and ensures oaths are kept.<br /> <br /> Teotl Worshipper: Our gods give of their blood and flesh to provide water and food and keep the sun ablaze. They ask for offerings, yes, but they do not ask for that which they are not willing to give. It's a divine pact.<br /> <br /> Deva Worshipper: So I danced for the entire day until my feet were numb but after Kali blessed me and helped my partner and I have a child together, it's a literal miracle!<br /> <br /> Mythos Worshipper: My God actively hates me and the only benefit I get from this is that when they try to kill everyone I'll get eaten first. Or ignored.<br /> <br /> Anunna Worshipper: Bruh my pantheon only recently started calling humanity their subjects instead of their slaves and <i>I</i> think that you gotta get out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, worshiping the Outer Gods would be like worshiping the Titans. In fact exactly the same, and we know that there are cults that worship the Titans and are about exactly like the cults worshiping Cthulhu in Lovecraft's tales. The Mythos are simply another group of Titans. With admittedly strange bells and whistles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T18:01:17-07:00","id":1399442,"title":"","content":"I've typed out and deleted like five different responses but ultimately... I don't see the point in putting in Cthulhu for the sake of Cthulhu, and I don't see the point in using the Mythos if you're putting it in a setting that they don't suit, thematically.<br /> <br /> Because then you're just putting them in for the meme value. Which yeah, I was in high school when Cthulhu started being a meme, that was like 15 years ago, so I guess I initially knew Cthulhu as nothing more than a joke, and then later I knew about the Mythos, academically, as a cosmic horror series.<br /> <br /> Like I'm working off and on on a setting hack that borrows elements from The Magnus Archive, a podcast I'm quite fond of that features Ancient Entities that are the fears of humanity, and Weird Stuff is the result of them brushing a bit too close to our world so that they can Feed. Would recommend.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER! I'm also making this hack with the assumption that there are no other Gods in this World, because their very thematic core doesn't work if they're defanged. Yes, the Slaughter represents the fear of senseless violence happening to you, but next to someone like Ares or Tyr, who could be that violence happening or protect you from it, then the entity of the Slaughter either gets crowded out by a more interesting being or it's not as scary when it's not being a bully.<br /> <br /> But really we're just spinning wheels again and again and again so I'm going to bow out. I'm definitely not gonna dispatch the Canon Ninjas if someone tries to put Cthulhu in their Scion games but I will <i>never</i> understand the appeal, because it seems to be taking the Mythos and using it in a way that <i>removes</i> its primary appeal: The horror aspect.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T18:18:03-07:00","id":1399448,"title":"","content":"I agree with you. I know there are options and all, but much of what Mythos represent is terror and insanity if what\u2019s beyond possible for the characters.<br /> If you limit to cultists and maybe sorcerers (hero level) it still makes sense as their power is far beyond (scales above) your reach and even your little power would drive you insane. It is not what Scion was made for, I mean, your character is locked to legend in all that is not Skills and Attributes, knacks, purview, birthrights (mainly when dealing with Origin).<br /> <br /> Yet, I like the concept, I will buy it (back it if KS happens) just for whatever they are bringing. It\u2019s not usual to play the other side of Mythos (the non mortal side) and, in the worst situation, I can adapt some to TC and play an investigative game with a system that fits better my taste (in opposition to CoC that is quite overwhelming to me)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T19:59:00-07:00","id":1399477,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz you both make some very good points. Ultimately I\u2019m gonna buy Masks of the Mythos when it comes out, read it carefully from cover to cover (or at least the important parts), and only then decide what (if anything) I want to do about combining Scion with the Cthulhu Mythos or creating a character for that setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T20:44:42-07:00","id":1399489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1399387#post1399387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Who would worship the Outer Gods?</i> These guys fucking suck from the perspective of a mortal. Like, how would that pitch meeting go between worshippers?</div> </div> </div> </div>The best answer I've ever seen to that question was Victor LaValle's <i>The Ballad of Black Tom</i>. <br /> <br /> Basically, revenge. You hate someone or something - even the entire state of the world and its power structure - so much that you don't care what it takes to destroy it. And my impression from Lovecraft's original stories is that they kind of presume that human gods - including God - don't really exist. So if you want something to actually answer your heartfelt prayers for vengeance, the Mythos is probably your best bet. <br /> How this would actually work in Scion, I have no idea. I'm guessing that it would have to presume the Theocentric dial being turned down to almost Zero/Hard Iron, with the Mythos the only game in town. And also probably that most of the Mythos's &quot;gods&quot; are classified as Titans. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T21:09:14-07:00","id":1399493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1399489#post1399489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, revenge. You hate someone or something - even the entire state of the world and its power structure - so much that you don't care what it takes to destroy it. And my impression from Lovecraft's original stories is that they kind of presume that human gods - including God - don't really exist. So if you want something to actually answer your heartfelt prayers for vengeance, the Mythos is probably your best bet.<br /> How this would actually work in Scion, I have no idea. I'm guessing that it would have to presume the Theocentric dial being turned down to almost Zero/Hard Iron, with the Mythos the only game in town. And also probably that most of the Mythos's &quot;gods&quot; are classified as Titans.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Eyep. Nobody would worship the Mythos Powers if there's literally any other option.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T21:15:47-07:00","id":1399495,"title":"","content":"I still think &quot;Thor, Durga, and Sun Wukong team up to punch Cthulhu in the face&quot; would make a fun campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T21:23:58-07:00","id":1399498,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> agreed!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T05:34:16-07:00","id":1399571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1399495#post1399495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think &amp;quot;Thor, Durga, and Sun Wukong team up to punch Cthulhu in the face&amp;quot; would make a fun campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you follow the latest critical thought maybe Ganesha, Hermes, Thoth, Mananan Mac Lir, and Athena, could make diplomatic contact with Yog-Sothoth to undermine Nyarlathotep and Cthulhu. <br /> <br /> By the way, as Cthulhu is imprisoned by submerging his city, I can't see him as a Sea God/ Water Elemental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T18:22:41-07:00","id":1399963,"title":"","content":"Just riffing on Astromancer;s comment around the sunken city... (he is now a drowned god of \u2026), that Having the Cthulhu gods as Titans, &quot;killed&quot; by the fall of Atlantis and the 1st ed. Atlantean gods felled by the same event. could be an interesting revisit of &quot;dead gods and titans&quot;, no worshipers, no war, just stagnant conflict, a failed experiment of Fate where each god had a Titan it fought and all died. Now awoken by young demigods on a quest to the Underworld, the disturbed titans and gods attempt to gain a foothold in the world and Overworld. Offering power to the downtrodden (looking at you Hercules), and attempting to ultimately conquer the Underworld, when they learn how much the Mythos has changed during their near slumber.<br /> <br /> I don't know, it could work for the right group. Though the Cthulhu gods are so alien, I imagine them being the Titans of an alien species, not humans. Which means that Humans are not the sole authors of Fate, but so are the Martians (or what ever aliens) created the doom of the Elder gods. Cthulhu could fear mortal Fate, trapping it to a Doom - maybe?<br /> <br /> Thanks for a post that made me respond, vs. just viewing and navigating away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T03:41:00-07:00","id":1400270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1389003#post1389003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are many versions of how the Old Ones are supposed to be. The original Lovecraft versions of the Old Ones are utterly indifferent to humanity in much the same way that you are indifferent to the huge amounts of bacteria and microorganisms you kill when you wash your hands with soap.<br /> <br /> The overly antagonistic versions you are talking about who are opposed by the more or less &amp;quot;good&amp;quot; Elder Gods is a conceit of the author August Derleth who infused quite a lot of his Catholic world-view into the mythos. Amongst Lovecraft fans he is not well-regarded for this reason. They mean it goes against the core of nihilism and atheism that is part of cosmic horror. I'm not saying Derleth's version is &amp;quot;incorrect&amp;quot; or inferior, but that is a pretty common view amongst the fans of Lovecraft.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Elder Gods protecting humanity were definitely a thing in the original Lovecraft. I don't think he used the term Elder Gods, but he did call them gods and they did appear in a few stories. As for the horrors being antagonistic, I don't think they ever were, but their mere existence has always been inimical to normal life. August Derleth may have expanded these ideas but he didnt invent them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T21:56:19-07:00","id":1400901,"title":"","content":"A large part of me thinks the Great Old Ones should be modelled/treated as Titans in Scion. They seem to tick all the appropriate boxes for it. I can't really picture them as a traditional pantheon.<br /> The Elder Gods illicit more complex thoughts and feelings.<br /> <br /> So I could, in theory see it play out as two rival pantheons, I'd rather have the Great Old Ones as a Titanmachy that the Elder Gods struggle to contain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T01:45:03-07:00","id":1400919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387060-mythos?p=1400901#post1400901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A large part of me thinks the Great Old Ones should be modelled/treated as Titans in Scion. They seem to tick all the appropriate boxes for it. I can't really picture them as a traditional pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree, +100 to this idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}